        "original_id": "a18581d3-7706-5ab3-ade3-6df030adefa1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Betzy Kjelsberg, Robert Hermansen\n- Places: Svelvik, Vestfold, Botne, Norway\n- Organizations: Liberal Party\n- Roles: politician, factory inspector, businessperson, feminist\n\nFacts:\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was born as Betzy Aleksandra Børresen on 1 November 1866 in Svelvik, Vestfold, Norway.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg was a Norwegian politician for the Liberal Party, the first female board member of the party, Norway’s first female factory inspector from 1910 to 1936, and a member of the feminist movement.\n- Robert Hermansen was born in 1939 in Botne, Vestfold, Norway.\n- Robert Hermansen is a Norwegian businessperson.\n- Vestfold is a county in Norway that borders Buskerud and Telemark.\n- Botne is a former municipality in Vestfold county, Norway.\n- Betzy Kjelsberg died on 3 October 1950.",
